* SL_NEED
* Screen library: is the window as big as a full-screen program is laid out for?
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 18 Oct 26 dm  New (terminal 140 by 42, phase 2).  One check and one message (11197) for every full-screen program of SD's
*               own, so that the size they insist on is stated in one place: SED now; the IDE and CED when their phase comes.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $sl_need(name, minw, minh, msg)
*
*     name        what the program is called in the message (SED)
*     minw minh   the size the program is laid out for
*     msg         returned: null when the window ($sl_window) is at least that big; else message 11197, "SED needs a window of
*                 at least 140 columns by 42 lines; this one is 100 by 30".  The program prints it (or STOPs with it) and does
*                 not start.
*
*   Only a program that is laid out for a size asks.  A user's SCREEN OPEN program asks for its own with MINSIZE w,h, and SD does
*   not impose 140 by 42 on it; the debugger's full-screen display falls back to line mode instead of refusing.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine sl_need(name, minw, minh, msg)
$catalog $sl_need

   call $sl_window(w, h)
   msg = ''
   if w < minw or h < minh then
      msg = sysmsg(11197, name, minw, minh, w : ' by ' : h)       ;* %1 needs a window of at least %2 columns by %3 lines; this one is %4
   end

   return
end

* END-CODE
